course: dictionary
lesson: 14483
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word pathetic has two main meanings. Read the sentence around it and ask: which meaning fits here?
explain: «That was a pathetic excuse, Sam. You forgot your homework again.» Here pathetic means very weak or poor, not good enough. It is informal and can be rude, so do not use it to hurt someone's feelings. Try swapping in "poor": "That was a poor excuse" still makes sense.
explain: «The pathetic little kitten sat alone in the rain, shivering.» Here pathetic means it makes you feel pity and sadness. Look at the clues: alone, shivering, in the rain. Nobody is being insulted; the kitten just looks sad and needs help.
fact: Pathetic is an adjective, so it describes a noun: a pathetic excuse, a pathetic attempt.
fact: «Pathetic» means very weak, useless or poor, and it is informal.
fact: «Pathetic» can also mean making you feel pity and sadness.
fact: «Pathetic» is often used as a rude insult, so think before you say it to someone.
fact: The comparative is more pathetic, as in «His drawing looked more pathetic after the rain.»
exercise: «Her pathetic excuse for being late did not convince anyone.» What does pathetic mean here? | *Very weak and not good enough | Full of pity for her | Bright and cheerful | Very loud
exercise: «The pathetic little puppy shivered under the bush, looking lost.» What does pathetic mean here? | *Making you feel pity and sadness | Very funny | Very fast | Very strong and brave
exercise: Which phrase could replace «a pathetic attempt» in a kinder way? | *A weak attempt | A brave attempt | A funny attempt | A fast attempt
test:
Why should you be careful when you use pathetic about a friend? | *It can be a rude insult | It means very happy | It is a name for a bird | It means very tall
test:
In «a pathetic little kitten in the rain», what feeling does pathetic show? | *Pity and sadness | Anger | Excitement | Boredom
exam:
What is the best check for the meaning of pathetic in «That was a pathetic excuse»? | *Swap in "poor" and see if the sentence still makes sense | Count the letters | Look only at the first word | Change it into a verb
